on":"Always 'suggested' (inactive) for a freshly-suggested audience."},"source":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"profileAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"The client PROFILE (WHO, a cold audience the client keeps or pauses on the Targeting page) this source list was built for: a buying-signal list (hiring now, new in role, recently funded) or a competitor-post engagement list finds THAT profile's people, screened against the profile's text. Pausing or archiving the profile pauses its lists; resuming it resumes them (unless the source itself is off). null on a profile itself, on a whole-ICP list built before profiles had their own (retired once they do), and on every other audience. Show profiles = rows with null here and channels[0].list = apollo_search; sources = channels[0].list."},"role":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"enum":["target","search",null],"description":"AUDIENCE-PER-OFFER-1107. 'target' = THE audience of its offer: its text is who the offer targets, it has no list of its own and finds people through the brand's lists, each person judged against its text. 'search' = a list of the brand (Apollo search, signals, engagement) walked by every offer audience of it; hidden from GET /orgs/audiences unless role=search. null = an audience as before."},"canonicalAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"When this audience is a deprecated provider-variant (e.g. retired '<base> [Apify]' from the apify->apollo migration), the id of its active canonical replacement. Membership/stats reads resolve a deprecated match to this audience. null for non-deprecated / unlinked rows."},"filters":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"additionalProperties":{"nullable":true}},"avatarUrl":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"Audience avatar as a hosted HTTP(S) URL. null until generated."},"apolloCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"apifyCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"countedAt":{"